WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.590
Two runners, A and B, set off
together along a long, straight path.

2
00:00:05.640 --> 00:00:09.490
As they run, their distance–time
graphs draw themselves.

3
00:00:09.540 --> 00:00:11.320
A's line is straight.

4
00:00:11.370 --> 00:00:14.340
B's starts steeper, then flattens.

5
00:00:14.390 --> 00:00:17.840
Then, at eight minutes,
the two lines cross.

6
00:00:17.890 --> 00:00:19.850
So what does that crossing mean?

7
00:00:19.900 --> 00:00:21.750
Are they running at the same speed?

8
00:00:21.800 --> 00:00:23.700
Has one runner stopped?

9
00:00:23.750 --> 00:00:28.470
In this mission, you'll read the gradient
of a distance–time graph as speed:

10
00:00:28.520 --> 00:00:30.770
distance divided by time.

11
00:00:30.820 --> 00:00:36.010
You'll see that steeper means faster,
and that a horizontal line means stopped.

12
00:00:36.060 --> 00:00:39.620
And you'll learn what it tells
you when two graphs cross.

13
00:00:39.670 --> 00:00:43.080
Your mission: explain what
the crossing point means.
